 "poem": "And, as a king mine hour,\nI will speak to thee alone in heaven,\nMy joy and grief, my love and shame alone.\nAnd thus shall life be ended,\nDay after day shall we abide,\nUnclouded of sorrow or light alone.\nIV. THE LIVING ARISE FROM DAWN Again.\nAs a leaf from a rising flower\nThat is set down on the flower\nAs upon the leaf above,\nIt would not seem old nor dead and dying,\nIf only it were left so lying.",
